A||N||18||Haze_Performance||Notchback with a GT bumper?||||14||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||11-14-2001||05:28 AM||||I'm thinking about GT-ing the '85 Coupe (without the fastback). Anyone have any pics of a Notchback with a 86/88 rear bumper? How about all round moldings too?<P><BR>Thanks<BR>-Haze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">   <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Wolfhound||11-14-2001||07:39 AM||||Haze, AlexFormula has just replaced the body pannels on an 88 Formula with aero panels and GT facias with round molding. I like the concept.<BR>Coy||||reg||14
Z||000002||MR2KLR||11-14-2001||08:15 AM||||do only fastbacks have round trim? Thought all 88's & 86-88 GT's had it?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||11-14-2001||08:22 AM||||No aero Notchbacks have round molding from the factory. 86-87 SE Notchbacks retained the groved molding and there were no aero Notchback 88s made only Coupes Formulas and GTs. <BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||11-14-2001||08:39 AM||||It's almost the same as the SE/85GT look. To keep my round moldings I put an 87GT rear bumper. In photos is hard to notice the ribbed trim. (see <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011682.html)." TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011682.html).</A> <BR>I liked better the round trim to keep it more 88ish. My trim is off now so I can't provide you pics.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChopTop||11-14-2001||08:40 AM||||Haze I just posted some pics in another thread, check out this thread to see a pic of a 88GT bumper on a 85.   <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010924-1-006355.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010924-1-006355.html</A> <P>All ribbed mouldings will be switched over to the smooth style.  I hope to paint the car by next summer, haven't decided on color yet, but moulding will be painted body color.<p>[This message has been edited by ChopTop (edited 11-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||11-14-2001||08:45 AM||||The fastback GT rear bumper and the 85 GT/86-87 bumpers are different aside from molding. The notchback has the rear set at a slight angle to match the angle of the tail lights. Where the fastback is more straight up and down to meet the angle of those tail lights.<BR>If you put a fastback rear on you will have a gap between the molding and the tail lights. I've seen it done and the gap isn't too bad, but I'd still use the notchback version. Unless you are wanting to change the molding to smooth.<P>All 86-88 fastback GT's, 87-88 coupes, and 88 Formula's have smooth molding.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||11-14-2001||10:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>If you put a fastback rear on you will have a gap between the molding and the tail lights. I've seen it done and the gap isn't too bad... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How big is the gap? <BR>I've been considering doing this on my 88 project car. Might have to reconsider.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Philphine||11-14-2001||11:01 AM||||i put an 86-88 gt rear on my 87 coupe. didn't notice much of a gap. i liked it. mine was damaged recently so i mean to do it again.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||11-14-2001||11:07 AM||||The angle difference exist but the gap must be very small because I haven't noticed it. Will check it today and take pics if possible.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000010||Alex4mula||11-14-2001||01:02 PM||||Well, at least in my 88 Formula chassis there is NO gap with the fastback rear bumper. Fit is perfect. Check the link for photos of both my Formulas rear. <A HREF="http://www.ofoto.com/I.jsp?m=51648385203&n=1853669559" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ofoto.com/I.jsp?m=51648385203&n=1853669559</A> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||6
Z||000011||MR2KLR||11-14-2001||01:11 PM||||So a '88 coupe has round trim, Right? So what fiero would I get a Areo Rear facia to match a '88 coupe? a Formula? or do thay have the coupe facia?<P> sory if I don't make sence I have only ever owned 84 SE's my first non-84 will be here on the 25th.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Hank is Here||11-14-2001||02:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MR2KLR:<BR><B>So a '88 coupe has round trim, Right? So what fiero would I get a Areo Rear facia to match a '88 coupe? a Formula? or do thay have the coupe facia?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>All the 88 coupe and Formula body parts are exactly the same!  The only difference is that the Formula has the spolier.  <BR>As far as I know all fastback GT's are round<BR>87-88 coupes/Formula are also round.  The 87 SE still has the ribbed style moulding||||reg||1
Z||000013||Alex4mula||11-14-2001||03:21 PM||||MR2KLR; 86-88 fastback rear aero fascia will match the 88 coupe round trim. Same for the front.<BR>On some years SEs you can use the front aero fascia by changing the bullet trim. Not sure which years because some has a ribbed part molded in.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||11-14-2001||04:24 PM||||Alex,<P>Thanks for posting the pics. Doesn't look like any more of a gap to me. As a matter of fact, my Formula seems to have more of a gap. Maybe it's just the luck of the draw. <BR>That's going to be a nice looking ride, too.<BR>Gonna paint it white?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||14
